<helpdocument version="1.0">
<meta>
<topic id="textscalc01func_bitrshiftxml" indexer="include" status="PUBLISH">
<title id="tit" xml-lang="en-US">BITRSHIFT</title>
<filename>/text/scalc/01/func_bitrshift.xhp</filename>
</topic>
</meta>
<body>
<bookmark xml-lang="en-US" branch="index" id="bm_id3160601">
<bookmark_value>BITRSHIFT function</bookmark_value>
<bookmark_value>bitwise right shift</bookmark_value>
</bookmark>
<bookmark xml-lang="en-US" branch="hid/SC_HID_FUNC_BITRSHIFT" id="bm_id3160602" localize="false"/>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160601" xml-lang="en-US" level="2" l10n="U"><variable id="bitrshift"><link href="text/scalc/01/func_bitrshift.xhp">BITRSHIFT</link>
</variable></paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160603" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><ahelp hid="HID_FUNC_BITRSHIFT">Bitwise right shift of an integer value.</ahelp> The bits of <emph>Number</emph> are shifted to the right by <emph>Shift</emph> positions, equivalent to dividing by 2 raised to the power of <emph>Shift</emph>.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160604" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="U">Syntax</paragraph>
<paragraph role="code" id="par_id3160605" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">BITRSHIFT(Number; Shift)</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160606" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><emph>Number</emph> is the integer value to be shifted. It must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than 2^48 (281474976710656).</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160607" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><emph>Shift</emph> is the number of bit positions to shift. A positive value shifts right; a negative value shifts left (the direction is reversed).</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160608" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="U">Remarks</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160609" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">If <emph>Shift</emph> is 0, <emph>Number</emph> is returned unchanged.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160610" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">If <emph>Shift</emph> is greater than or equal to 64 (or less than or equal to -64), the result is 0.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160611" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><emph>Number</emph> is truncated to an integer before the operation. Non-integer, negative, or out-of-range values for <emph>Number</emph>, or non-finite values for <emph>Shift</emph>, return an error (Err:502).</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160612" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U">Example: decimal 8 is binary <quote>1000</quote>. BITRSHIFT(8; 2) shifts right by 2, giving binary <quote>10</quote>, which is decimal 2.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3160613" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="U">Example</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160614" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><item type="input">=BITRSHIFT(8; 2)</item> returns 2.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160615" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><item type="input">=BITRSHIFT(1; -2)</item> returns 4 because a negative shift reverses direction and shifts left by 2.</paragraph>
<embed href="text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#siehe"/>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3160616" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="U"><link href="text/scalc/01/func_bitlshift.xhp" name="BITLSHIFT">BITLSHIFT</link>.</paragraph>
</body>
</helpdocument>
